{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150813-home-brew-artifact-for-comments-and-criticism","id":1150813,"title":"Home brew artifact for comments and criticism.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-18T15:36:45-07:00","id":1150813,"title":"Home brew artifact for comments and criticism.","content":"Hi all, I am running a first Rd VtR game using clans and gen from VtM, I have developed an artifact to help give my players a power boost (they are all BP1 Gen 13) and to see what they would do with it. Any comments and criticisms would be great.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bloodstone Chalice </u></b><br /> A large sandstone chalice with the interior studded with Bloodstones. The exterior is polished smooth, while the interior is rough stone.<br /> The interior is blood stained with some blood encrusted part way up the sides, and congealed blood in the very bottom.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The Bloodstone Chalice has two effects, the first is when vitae from multiple kindred is willingly put into the chalice, mixed drunk by those who put their vitae into the chalice, the drinkers Generation is reduced by One, this can only happen once per drinker. This will cause a level one vininculum to form.<br /> <br /> The second effect is that blood or Vitae (this will render the vitae neutral, and unable to form a blood bond) from any source no matter how old will provide sustenance to any kindred who drinks it, no matter what their feeding restrictions, this will provide on Vitae to the drinker, this is limited to one Vitae per day per kindred.<br /> <br /> With both of these effects there is no risk of the user forming an addiction to Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T03:42:20-07:00","id":1150946,"title":"","content":"Is the reduction in generation permanent?<br /> Are vinculums permanent in this game?<br /> <br /> This kind of looks like some random oddity that would be used by someone with a significant feeding restriction in an emergency. Need diseased or potent blood? Just dump a pint of cat blood in the chalice and done.<br /> &quot;Maybe&quot; it's held by a Theban or Cruac ritualist for blood orgies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T04:44:12-07:00","id":1150952,"title":"","content":"I see the generation reduction and the vinculum from the artifact being permanent.<br /> <br /> I have the idea that so much vitae has been put into this chalice that the first effect is something that was never thought about until so early neonates got hold of it and experimented with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T05:46:39-07:00","id":1150967,"title":"","content":"The thing I'd wonder about is what effect higher generation will actually have. <br /> <br /> Does your version of generation have the same impact on Dominate as it did in Masquerade? For a Ventrue, that'd be an interesting change, suddenly your sire can't dominate you on a whim.<br /> <br /> Also, are Gen 14 vampires still thin-bloods? (I can't actually remember if gen 14 were still full kindred or not) A boost to gen 12 would allow your players to start siring full vampires which would be an interesting step up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:03:26-07:00","id":1151011,"title":"","content":"It's hard to comment on balance unless we know more about how you're implementing generation within VtR.<br /> <br /> As a utility item I can see it as being of great value to many people--and the kind of thing that would be created by someone, at some point, if they could figure out how (likely Theban or Cruac sorcerers). In other words, it makes sense to exist and is merely one of many work-arounds for feeding restrictions... one that can be stolen!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T15:50:52-07:00","id":1151139,"title":"","content":"For my game I have linked generation and blood potency, with BP being how much vitae you can hold and use, with generation being your max skill, attributes, and discipline. For the most part they will be at the same level, but some effects might raise your BP for a short time or even be permanent, and torpor would keep the generation the same but lower the BP as the requiem rule book.<br /> <br /> As for disciplines I'm using either the requiem rule book or the translation guide (even if I might transfer over to v20 when I can afford to get the hardback)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:43:59-07:00","id":1152318,"title":"","content":"Wrong game dude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T03:04:47-07:00","id":1152445,"title":"","content":"Not really, if you cared to read you have seen that they are using a mix of Masquerade and Requiem elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T06:46:29-07:00","id":1152786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drofkcah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1150813-home-brew-artifact-for-comments-and-criticism?p=1151139#post1151139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my game I have linked generation and blood potency, with BP being how much vitae you can hold and use, with generation being your max skill, attributes, and discipline. For the most part they will be at the same level, but some effects might raise your BP for a short time or even be permanent, and torpor would keep the generation the same but lower the BP as the requiem rule book.<br /> <br /> As for disciplines I'm using either the requiem rule book or the translation guide (even if I might transfer over to v20 when I can afford to get the hardback)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ignore the threadcrapping. Your approach is entirely viable and will produce a somewhat lower-power game on one end, and higher-power on the other (elders). The tension from Masquerade will remain: &quot;how do I overcome the impossible heights of the scary ancients?&quot; That tension in Requiem is purposefully toned-down somewhat, making elder less unassailable and their requiems more fragile. Especially after torpor.<br /> <br /> Good luck!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T12:23:46-07:00","id":1154181,"title":"","content":"The players are currently trying to find their place in kindred society, they are trying to make themselves useful so the Prince doesn't just order their final death (they were sired to be sabbat shovelheads) so the game is definitely getting interesting for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:28:07-07:00","id":1154203,"title":"","content":"Is the idea that the group vinculum will make that task more difficult? I mean, that makes the group look a bit like a Sabbat pack.<br /> <br /> Have you given much thought to the history of the artefact?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T14:30:19-07:00","id":1154226,"title":"","content":"If Generation works the same way in your game as it did in Masquerade, strengthening it by one has much greater effect on Elders than it does on Neonates. The difference is teensy for 13th-Gens, but a 4th-Gen Methuselah could theoretically become an Antedeluvian. Even other ancient Vampires would like to own the Artifact to circumvent feeding restrictions. If knowledge of the Chalice spreads, your characters will find themselves in ground zero of a disaster, with everyone and their mother wanting the Artifact for themselves. That doesn't even account for unexpected quirks the Chalice might manifest in edge cases. In other words, sounds like fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T15:37:16-07:00","id":1154529,"title":"","content":"The vinculum is one way to stop it becoming too powerful, I'm also thinking about giving the gen lowering effect a limit. I've not really given much thought to the history, I'm thinking that it might have been made by a tremere elder as a way of ensuring a constant supply of vitae. The lowering of the gen is an accidental secondary effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T05:20:08-07:00","id":1154669,"title":"","content":"Even if we assume the Chalice won't reduce Generation below 8th, it's still a massive deal. It could be used to uplift Thin-bloods to standard Vampirehood, which has massive political and religious ramifications. In a way, the secondary effect is more notable than the intended one. Vampires have been getting blood for millenia, but decreasing Generation without Diablerie is something unique.<br /> <br /> A level one Vinculum is not that big a deal compared to that, especially since you can use blood of someone expendable, and then kill them. Perhaps you might make the Vinculum count towards the Chalice itself, and whatever mysterious agenda an object might have. The strengthening of Generation may also depend on the continued existence of the Chalice, meaning those who benefited from it need to keep it safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T05:49:42-07:00","id":1154677,"title":"","content":"That's definitely some things to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19303-drofkcah","name":"Drofkcah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}